Yes.  You should not eat dwarfs, dwarf lords or dwarf kings.  Those
are the only things that would make you a cannibal.

> So how can Heidi get to Medusa?  She has a couple of wands of cold
> (charges unknown); can she freeze a path and walk across that?  Is
> there something else we're missing?

That's one way.  It's said that the level with Medusa's island in the
middle is reachable with jumping boots or the jumping spell (at
sufficiently high escape spell skills).  There is an amulet that would
allow you to safely walk underwater.  Of course, your iron items can
rust, your potions dilute and your scrolls/spellbooks blank, but those
are all preventable with the right equipment.

With polymorph control and a means of polymorphing, you could change
into a creature that flies/swims.  Be careful of your armor first and
make sure you get across as fast as possible (before you turn back to
a dwarf over the water).  Vampires can wear normal armor and fly
(beware cockatrices) and are a good choice for a human-sized flying
monster.
 
> OTOH, now that I think about it, is digging down and then coming
> back up a better solution?

You can dig down, come back up (blinded), kill Medusa and see if
Perseus' statue contains cursed levitation boots.  Or, if you have a
way into a castle (musical instrument and the right tune, wands of
striking and cold), you could go in there and get the wand of wishing.

Finally, if you've done the quest and have teleport control, you can
invoke the Orb of Fate and teleport down a level (similar to digging,
but doesn't leave a hole)... ditto with a cursed scroll of
teleportation, or being confused as you read any scroll of
teleportation.
 
